 "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build of payments-service was failing because tests/test_money.py expects banker's rounding, but src/money.py used ROUND_HALF_UP.\n\nChange: `round_money` now quantizes with `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` instead of `ROUND_HALF_UP`, matching the docstring and FIN-212.\n\nVerification: CI passed on commit 08d3cd5986 (run ci-0001). Test expectations check out under half-even: 2.675 -> 2.68, 2.665 -> 2.66.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-pr-fix-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The nightly failure is fixed and PR #101 is open against main, with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **Change:** On branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding` I switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- **PR:** #101, \"Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212\", https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner under org policy, so that is still outstanding.", "type": "text"}]}]}